{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg --files /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/8 && find /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/8 -maxdepth 2 -type f | sort | xargs -r -I{} sh -c 'echo \\\"FILE:{}\\\"; sed -n \\\"1,220p\\\" \\\"{}\\\"'\"","aggregated_output":"/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/8/prompt.md\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/8/des.md\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/8/ids.txt\nFILE:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/8/des.md\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据封闭围栏内部的染色区域形状，选取匹配的印章模板，将其盖印到围栏的缺口外侧。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干由同一颜色（如 blue）像素构成的封闭矩形围栏，每个围栏恰好有一个单像素宽的缺口（即围栏边框上缺少一个像素）。\n  - 每个围栏内部有一小块由另一种颜色（如 red、green、yellow 等各不相同）填充的连通区域，形状各异（如 L 形、T 形、直线等），均为少量像素组成的小图案。\n  - 网格的某个角落区域有一排\"印章模板\"：每个模板是一个与围栏内部同尺寸的小网格，其中画有一种特定形状，颜色为 grey，模板之间用 maroon 像素分隔。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个围栏，提取其内部的染色区域形状（忽略颜色，只看形状）。\n  - 在印章模板区找到与该形状完全匹配（允许旋转 0°/90°/180°/270°）的模板。\n  - 确定围栏缺口所在的方向（上/下/左/右）。\n  - 将匹配到的模板以围栏内部染色区域的颜色，绘制在围栏缺口外侧，紧贴缺口，向外延伸（模板的一边与缺口对齐）。\n  - 围栏、内部染色区域、其他围栏及印章模板区均保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：需要两层独立推理——第一层是通过形状匹配（而非颜色）将围栏内部图案与印章模板配对；第二层是缺口方向决定了盖印的位置和朝向，而盖印颜色来源于围栏内部的染色颜色而非模板本身的 grey。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将散落的彩色路径片段按颜色拼合为完整路径，再沿每条完整路径的行进方向依次放置该路径经过的路标颜色序列。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干条由不同颜色像素组成的一像素宽路径片段，每条路径片段是水平或垂直的直线段，长度不等。同一颜色的片段属于同一条逻辑路径，但被打散分布在网格各处。\n  - 每条路径片段的某些像素位置上叠放有\"路标\"像素——用另一种与路径颜色不同的颜色标记（如路径为 blue，路标可能是 red 或 green）。路标颜色在整个网格中可能重复出现在不同路径上。\n  - 网格底部有一排与路径颜色数量相同的空矩形框（由 grey 像素围成），每个框内部为背景色，框的宽度等于对应路径上路标的数量，高度为 1。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每种路径颜色，将所有同色片段在空间上拼接（片段的端点恰好相邻），还原出一条从一端到另一端的完整路径。\n  - 确定路径的行进方向：路径的起点是不与任何同色片段相邻的那个端点（即度为 1 的端点中，行坐标或列坐标更小的那个为起点）。\n  - 沿行进方向遍历完整路径上的每个像素，按顺序收集遇到的路标颜色。\n  - 将收集到的路标颜色序列从左到右填入底部对应颜色框内（框与路径的对应关系通过框边框下方的一个单像素颜色标记确定，该标记颜色等于路径颜色）。\n\n- `Key insight`：第一层推理是将分散的同色路径片段在空间上拼合成唯一的完整路径；第二层推理是确定路径的有向遍历顺序，并按该顺序提取路标颜色；第三层是通过框下方的颜色标记将路径与输出框配对。片段拼接需要空间邻接推理，而非简单的颜色分类。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在镜像对称的双面板中，找出每一侧独有的差异像素，然后将左侧差异像素的颜色涂到右侧差异像素的位置，反之亦然。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 网格被一条垂直的 maroon 单像素宽分隔线分为左右两个面板，两侧面板尺寸相同。\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 两个面板各包含由多种颜色组成的图案，两侧图案整体呈左右镜像对称，但各有若干像素与镜像位置不同：要么颜色不同，要么一侧有像素而镜像位置为背景色。\n  - 差异像素的数量在左右两侧相同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 将右面板沿分隔线做左右镜像翻转，与左面板逐像素比较。\n  - 找出所有不匹配的位置（差异位置）。\n  - 对于左面板中每个差异位置：将该位置的颜色记录下来，然后将该像素改为其在右面板镜像对应位置的颜色。\n  - 对于右面板中每个差异位置：将该位置的颜色改为其在左面板镜像对应位置的原始颜色。\n  - 即左右差异像素的颜色互换（交换后两面板变为完美镜像对称）。\n  - 分隔线和所有非差异像素保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者首先需要识别出两面板之间的对称关系是镜像而非平移；然后需要发现变换不是简单地\"修复\"对称（例如删除多余像素），而是将两侧的差异颜色互换——这意味着输出中两面板变为完美对称，但用的是对方的颜色而非自己的。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中每个彩色箭头沿其指向方向发射，箭头穿过同色\"传送门\"像素时改变行进方向，最终在停止位置绘制箭头。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干个由 3 个像素组成的箭头形状，每个箭头由一个\"头部\"像素和两个\"翼部\"像素构成。箭头指向四个基本方向之一（上/下/左/右）：\n    - 指向右的箭头：头部在右，两翼在头部左侧的上下两格。\n    - 指向下的箭头：头部在下，两翼在头部上方的左右两格。\n    - 其余方向类推。\n  - 每个箭头有自己的颜色（如 red、blue、green 等）。\n  - 网格中散布若干单像素的\"传送门\"标记，每个传送门的颜色与某个箭头相同。同色传送门总是成对出现（恰好 2 个）。\n  - 网格边界处可能有 grey 像素构成的墙壁。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 擦除每个箭头的原始位置（变为背景色）。\n  - 每个箭头沿其指向方向逐格移动（头部像素沿方向前进）。\n  - 当箭头的头部像素到达同色传送门之一时，箭头的头部立即出现在另一个同色传送门的位置，并且行进方向旋转 90 度顺时针。\n  - 箭头继续沿新方向移动，直到头部碰到网格边缘或 grey 墙壁像素（头部将到达的下一个位置超出边界或为墙壁），此时箭头停止。\n  - 在停止位置绘制箭头（保持最终朝向和原始颜色）。传送门像素保留不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：第一层推理需要从箭头的 3 像素形状中解读出朝向信息；第二层需要发现同色传送门的配对传送机制以及传送后方向固定旋转 90 度顺时针的规则；解题者必须在样例中追踪箭头的完整轨迹才能归纳出传送+旋转的组合规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在由色块组成的棋盘格局中，根据每个色块内部\"种子\"像素的数量，将该色块按同心层方式由外向内逐层剥离并重新着色。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 网格由若干个大小不等的矩形色块紧密拼接而成，无背景色（所有像素都属于某个色块）。\n  - 每个矩形色块是单色填充的实心矩形，颜色各不相同（如 red、blue、green、yellow 等）。\n  - 每个色块内部散布有若干个 orange 单像素\"种子\"标记（数量为 1 到 4 不等）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个矩形色块，数出其内部 orange 种子像素的数量 N（N 取值 1-4）。\n  - 将该色块重新绘制为 N 层同心矩形环：\n    - 最外层环保持色块的原始颜色。\n    - 从外向内，每层环依次使用一个固定的颜色循环序列：原色 → grey → azure → maroon（若 N=1 则整个色块保持原色不变；若 N=2 则最外一层原色、内部全部 grey；若 N=3 则外层原色、中间层 grey、最内层 azure；若 N=4 则四层分别为原色、grey、azure、maroon）。\n    - 每层环的宽度为 1 像素。若色块太小导致无法容纳 N 层完整环，则从最内层开始省略，优先保留外层。\n  - 种子像素在输出中被覆盖（不保留）。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者首先需要识别出网格是由紧密拼接的矩形色块构成的（而非背景上的独立对象）；然后需要发现种子数量决定了同心环的层数，而非决定颜色或大小；最后需要归纳出固定的颜色循环序列。三个发现缺一不可，且种子数量的视觉作用（控制分层深度）与直觉中\"种子=生长\"的隐喻不同，增加了机制的隐蔽性。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：识别网格中被遮挡的多层十字形图案，根据遮挡关系确定层序，然后按从底层到顶层的顺序将每层十字的颜色输出为一列色条。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干个不同颜色的十字形图案（每个十字由一个中心像素向上下左右各延伸相同长度的臂构成，臂长为 2 像素，因此每个十字为 5x5 范围内的加号形，共 9 个像素）。\n  - 十字形图案之间存在重叠，上层十字的像素覆盖下层十字的像素。\n  - 网格右侧有一个由 grey 像素围成的空竖直矩形框，高度等于十字的数量，宽度为 1 像素。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 识别每种前景颜色对应的十字形图案：每种颜色的可见像素都位于某个十字模板的平移位置上。\n  - 对于每个十字，检查其模板上被其他颜色覆盖的像素——覆盖者在被覆盖者之上。\n  - 据此建立从底层到顶层的完整层序。\n  - 在右侧 grey 框内，从上到下依次填入从底层到顶层的十字颜色（每格填一种颜色）。\n\n- `Key insight`：这道题结合了从遮挡碎片还原完整图案并排序的层序推理与输出为颜色排列而非空间图案的输出形式，但使用了不同的基础图元（十字形）。解题者需要先从部分可见像素中推断出每个十字的完整位置，再利用重叠处的颜色信息推断层序——两步推理都非平凡。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中每个\"容器\"对象内部的散落像素收集起来，按照容器开口方向将它们重新排列为紧密堆叠在容器底部的矩形块。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（black）。\n  - 网格中有若干个由 blue 像素构成的 U 形或 C 形\"容器\"对象，每个容器由三面封闭墙壁构成，有一个方向的开口（上/下/左/右）。容器内部空间为矩形区域。\n  - 每个容器内部散布有若干个非背景色的彩色像素（同一容器内所有彩色像素颜色相同，但不同容器内颜色不同），这些像素在容器内部空间中随机分布。\n  - 容器外部没有彩色像素。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 确定每个容器的开口方向（缺少墙壁的那一侧）。\n  - \"底部\"定义为与开口相反的那一侧墙壁。\n  - 数出容器内部彩色像素的总数 N。\n  - 擦除容器内部所有彩色像素的原始位置。\n  - 将 N 个同色像素重新排列为紧贴底部墙壁的紧密矩形块：先填满紧贴底部的一行（沿底部墙壁的全宽），若像素有剩余则继续向开口方向填充下一行，最后一行可以不满（不满的行从左侧或上侧开始填充，即按行优先、列递增的顺序）。\n  - 容器墙壁和背景保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要首先识别容器的开口方向（这决定了\"重力\"的方向），然后理解变换是\"将散落像素沉淀到底部\"的紧密堆积过程。关键的非显然之处在于\"底部\"不是全局的下方，而是每个容器各自的相对方向——不同容器可能有不同的\"重力方向\"，这使得解题者不能套用简单的\"所有东西往下掉\"的模式。\n</new_puzzle>\nFILE:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/8/ids.txt\neval/7b0280bc\ntrain/a644e277\ntrain/1a244afd\ntrain/8618d23e\ntrain/9b5080bb\ntrain/985ae207\neval/9aaea919\neval/80a900e0\neval/8e5c0c38\ntrain/aaef0977\ntrain/458e3a53\ntrain/df9fd884\ntrain/652646ff\neval/6e453dd6\ntrain/230f2e48\neval/8b7bacbf\ntrain/963c33f8\neval/5545f144\ntrain/22425bda\ntrain/f341894c\nFILE:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed807260302/8/prompt.md\n你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"7b0280bc\" lines=\"54-69\">\n<description>\nRecolor the shortest path between two terminal squares in a square-and-track graph.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Two non-bg colors form solid NxN squares (N>=2): one color marks exactly 2 terminals, the other marks stations.\n- A third non-bg color forms 1-cell-wide track segments connecting pairs of squares (graph edges).\n\nRule:\n- Find the shortest path (fewest edges) between the two terminal squares.\n- Recolor every station square on that path to green.\n- Recolor every track segment along that path to grey.\n- Everything else unchanged.\n\nKey insight: The grid encodes a graph where squares are nodes and tracks are edges; the task is graph shortest-path, not spatial proximity.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"a644e277\" lines=\"31-50\">\n<description>\nExtract the lattice subregion bounded by the four background-colored corner holes.\n\nInput structure:\n- A regular one-cell-thick lattice has one line color, one background color,\n  and sparse marker pixels.\n- Exactly four lattice-line intersections are background-colored holes instead\n  of line-color pixels.\n\nRule:\n- Find the unique non-background color that forms regular horizontal and\n  vertical lattice lines.\n- Use the four background-colored lattice intersections as the corners of one\n  rectangle.\n- Return the inclusive crop between those corner rows and columns.\n\nKey insight:\n- The crop is marked by the missing lattice intersections, not by the marker\n  pixels inside the cells.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"1a244afd\" lines=\"49-68\">\n<description>\nRotate each magenta source pixel 90 degrees counterclockwise around its matched blue pivot, recoloring the new pixel orange.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- The only foreground colors are blue pivot pixels and magenta source pixels.\n- Each magenta source can be paired one-to-one with a blue pivot in the same\n  row or column.\n\nRule:\n- Remove all magenta source pixels.\n- For each matched source/pivot pair, preserve the source distance from the\n  pivot but rotate its offset 90 degrees counterclockwise.\n- Paint the rotated in-bounds target orange; if the target is outside the\n  grid, the source simply disappears.\n\nKey insight:\nThe blue pixels are rotation centers, and row/column alignment gives a\nunique global matching from each magenta source to its pivot.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8618d23e\" lines=\"9-25\">\n<description>\nStagger the two horizontal input regions onto a larger maroon separator canvas.\n\nInput structure:\n- The input is a rectangular grid with an even number of rows.\n- The top half and bottom half are the two regions to preserve.\n- Maroon is absent from the input and is used only as the new separator color.\n\nRule:\n- Create an output with one extra row and one extra column, filled with maroon.\n- Copy the top half into the upper-left corner.\n- Copy the bottom half one row below the top region and one column to the right.\n\nKey insight:\nThe output is not a recoloring of either region; it inserts an L-shaped maroon\ngap by diagonally offsetting the lower half from the upper half.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9b5080bb\" lines=\"161-172\">\n<description>\nRecolor the small defect bars on each shared-color object with the opposite panel color.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid contains two large panel colors and one shared object color.\n- Each shared-color object is a mostly solid rectangle inside exactly one panel.\nRule\n- Find the near-solid rectangular core of each object.\n- Missing core pixels and one-cell protrusions define two-pixel bars perpendicular to the nearest core edge.\n- Recolor those bars with the other panel color; leave all other pixels unchanged.\nKey insight\n- The colors to add are not tied to numeric ids: each object's surrounding panel identifies the opposite panel color.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"985ae207\" lines=\"82-97\">\n<description>\nRepeat each 3x3 control-center sprite toward the matching solid rectangle until a copy first overlaps that rectangle.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Each sprite is a 3x3 foreground object whose eight border pixels have one color and whose center has a different control color.\n- For every control color, there is exactly one separate solid rectangular object of that color.\n\nRule\n- Match each sprite to the unique solid rectangle whose color equals the sprite center.\n- Copy the whole 3x3 sprite in the cardinal direction of that rectangle, stepping by three cells each time.\n- Stop after pasting the first copy whose 3x3 bbox overlaps the rectangle; copied pixels overwrite the rectangle there.\n\nKey insight\nThe center pixel is not the paint color: it is a destination key, while the entire 3x3 sprite is the motif tiled along the straight path.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"9aaea919\" lines=\"38-51\">\n<description>\nTransfer sprites from red-marked lanes to green-marked lanes, recoloring and stacking.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Red (2) and green (3) thin bars define vertical lanes.\n- Each lane contains repeated identical monochrome sprites in an evenly spaced vertical grid.\n\nRule:\n- Each red lane's sprites turn grey (5); their count transfers to the nearest green lane.\n- New sprites fill empty lattice slots bottom-up, using the source shape recolored to the destination lane's sprite color.\n- All marker bars are removed.\n\nKey insight: Sprite count is conserved across lanes — red sprites become grey, and equally many new sprites stack into the green lane's regular grid.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"80a900e0\" lines=\"69-82\">\n<description>\nExtend diagonal rays outward from outer-border segments adjacent to diamond shapes on a checkerboard.\n\nInput structure:\n- Checkerboard bg (two most common colors).\n- Hollow diamond outlines (8-pixel) in a non-bg color (inner border).\n- Short diagonal line segments in another non-bg color adjacent to each diamond edge (outer border).\n\nRule:\n- For each outer-border segment, determine the outward direction (perpendicular to the segment, away from the diamond).\n- From each endpoint of the segment, cast a diagonal ray outward, painting over bg pixels with the segment's color until hitting a non-bg pixel or the grid edge.\n\nKey insight: Rays emit only from the two endpoints of each outer-border segment, not every pixel, and travel diagonally away from the diamond.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8e5c0c38\" lines=\"9-21\">\n<description>\nClean each color layer by enforcing vertical mirror symmetry.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. Several non-bg colors, each forming a nearly-symmetric pattern about some vertical axis.\n- Some pixels in each color are \"noise\" that breaks the symmetry.\n\nRule:\n- For each non-bg color, find the vertical axis that best explains its pixel layout.\n- Remove any pixel that lacks a same-color mirror counterpart across that axis.\n\nKey insight: Each color has its own independent symmetry axis; the task is per-color denoising, not whole-grid symmetry.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"aaef0977\" lines=\"25-41\">\n<description>\nReplace an orange canvas with concentric Manhattan-distance color rings centered on the lone marker pixel.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is an orange background with exactly one non-orange marker pixel.\n- The marker color is one of the colors in the fixed non-orange ring cycle.\n\nRule:\n- The marker location is distance 0 and keeps the marker color.\n- Each step of Manhattan distance away from the marker advances one position\n  through the cycle green, yellow, black, grey, red, teal, maroon, pink, blue.\n- Fill every pixel of the original grid by this distance-indexed cycle.\n\nKey insight: The output is not copied from existing objects; it is the\ndistance field around the single marker, colored by a cyclic palette that\nexcludes the orange background.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"458e3a53\" lines=\"19-32\">\n<description>\nExtract the compact table of solid cells hidden inside a separator lattice.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has full-width and full-height bars of one separator color, dividing it into rectangular cells.\n- Most cells contain a repeating multicolor pattern, while a contiguous rectangle of cells is solid monochrome.\n\nRule\n- Split the input into lattice cells using the full separator rows and columns.\n- Keep the cells whose full interior is one color, crop to their occupied rectangle, and output those colors.\n\nKey insight\n- The periodic pattern is noise; only completely solid lattice cells encode the reduced output grid.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"df9fd884\" lines=\"33-47\">\n<description>\nMove the colored object from the lower bracket lane to the upper bracket lane and drop it to the bottom edge.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
